{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling under docs/kernel.md sections 7 and 7.1: the Live level.\n\nHugh placed the Live level in the stable base on 10 November (order\nfc7576f8). Section 7.1 of docs/kernel.md holds a new level while a K\nitem is open. K1, K4, K5, K6 and K10 are open, and the level closes\nnone of them.\n\nI rule:\n1. The first version of the Live level does not wait under section\n   7.1. The owner's decision is the reason. The exception covers the\n   first version that the Live note cuts, and nothing else.\n2. A live scope is an ordinary scope that writes its genesis entry\n   and its creator's confirmation, and no entry after them. Its\n   reference is the reference of any scope.\n3. The kernel part is small: the validator admits `live` version 1\n   and refuses the durable forms, and the fold refuses an entry after\n   a live scope's confirmation. The code that runs live acts is a\n   platform service. No recorded entry depends on it, so it passes\n   the test of section 2.\n4. The level adds no scope kind, platform name, capability, entry\n   kind, field type or kind of reference. It adds nothing to K1 or\n   K4.\n5. The head for request bf1992ae records this ruling in\n   docs/kernel.md, sections 7 and 7.1. The checker's review of that\n   head is the review that section 7 requires. If the checker refuses\n   the exception, the level waits and I return to Hugh.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}